DESCRIPTION:Some qualities are not values easily read off form the world\, 
 like a temperature or number. How do you measure\, track\, represent and d
 rive engineering quality\, without crudely reducing it to something it is 
 not?\n\nIn my work in Canonical's Engineering Excellence organisation\, I 
 direct engineering practice at scale: the documentation efforts of dozens 
 of teams in over a hundred software products. To do that I have had to fin
 d ways to measure quality of practice and outcome. I also had to persuade 
 all those engineering teams to accept them\, and work with them.\n\nThe me
 thods and approaches I developed for documentation have been adopted for o
 ther engineering disciplines\, such as security engineering practice. I'll
  share them in this workshop in the form of reusable tools that can simila
 rly be adopted and adapted to other needs. At the heart of them is a matur
 ity model that helps drive practice quality at scale\, elevating standards
 \, discipline and execution.\n\nI'll work with attendees to turn these too
 ls into tools for their own needs\, in their own companies and organisatio
 ns.
